---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Heading } from '../components/ui/Heading';
import { Container } from '../components/ui/Container';
import { Stack } from '../components/ui/Stack';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Chidi Onyema" description="Principal Backend Engineer. 10+ years building distributed systems. London-based, remote-friendly.">
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <Container size="prose">
      <Stack gap={12}>
        <div>
          <Heading variant="hero" level={1}>About</Heading>
          <p class="text-xl text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-6">
            Backend engineer in London. 10+ years. I work on payment systems,
            order platforms, and the infrastructure between them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-primary max-w-none">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Why I built this</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            A few years ago I was on a team where a deploy took out the message
            broker. Customers were charged but orders were never created. No
            alerts fired. It took three days to find the root cause: unconfirmed
            messages were lost on restart, and there was no outbox.
          </p>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            Since then I have been focused on making sure that does not happen.
            This portfolio exists so I can show the work rather than just
            describe it.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Focus areas</h2>
          <ul class="text-secondary space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Cross-service transactions</strong> that complete fully or roll back cleanly.</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic failure recovery</strong> so a crashed service does not leave orphaned data.</li>
            <li><strong>Financial correctness</strong> with double-entry bookkeeping and balance invariants.</li>
            <li><strong>Compile-time enforcement</strong> of architecture rules (159 CI guards, 50 Roslyn analyzers).</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">The platform</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            8 .NET 9 microservices on Fly.io, PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, Redis.
            Source is on
            <a href="https://github.com/chidionyema/haworks-platform" target="_blank" class="text-accent hover:underline">GitHub</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Education</h2>
          <ul class="text-secondary space-y-2">
            <li><strong>AI and Machine Learning</strong>, Professional Certificate, Imperial College Business School (2024)</li>
            <li><strong>Computer Science BSc (Hons)</strong>, Queen Mary University of London</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Stack</h2>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 not-prose">
            {['C# / .NET 9', 'MassTransit', 'EF Core', 'PostgreSQL', 'RabbitMQ', 'Redis', 'Polly', 'HashiCorp Vault', 'Docker', 'Fly.io', 'OpenTelemetry', 'xUnit', 'Pact', 'Aspire'].map(tech => (
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface-warm border border-border rounded text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider font-mono text-muted">{tech}</span>
            ))}
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Availability</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            Available for contract work. London or remote.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold bg-primary text-base-inverse hover:bg-secondary transition-all">
              Get in touch
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </Stack>
    </Container>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
